  "methodology": [
    "Before/after use the same captured 384 \u00d7 308 world:881 units,2503 buildings,1023 fields, original viewport and 2\u00d7 game speed. Separate local game instances leave the user running game untouched.",
    "Each replay uses the actual requestAnimationFrame main loop, simulation, Pixi rendering, HUD, and autosave. Five paused render warmup frames load assets. Final comparisons are unprofiled; no other tests or browser benchmarks run concurrently.",
    "FPS includes the first live cold-cache frame; steady work/interval percentiles exclude only that first frame, which is reported separately. Work duration and display interval differ because vsync rounds render opportunities.",
    "Road replay moves a real captured pointer 8 times per second across 12 endpoints, displays a 14 cell route, and releases to purchase 3 newroadcells. The measurement includes every queued purchase and cleanup frame until completion.",
    "Timing schema 3 separates input and queued construction from simulation. Older schema 1 includes input in simulation; compare total work/FPS across schemas. This does not affect the matched no-input comparison.",
    "Food deliveries, movement, and game-clock advance verify that higherFPS does not come from disabling gameplay or slowing the simulation materially."
  ],
